a three-year-long investigation in the  gambia has recommended former president  yahya jammeh be put on trial for murder  torture and sexual violence  best responsibility for the killing  of both alma mo mane and  the former president seized power in  1994 and for 22 years oversaw a regime  that has been accused of committing  hundreds of human rights abuses  [Music]  in 2017 xiaomi was forced into exile in  equatorial guinea after losing an  election to adama barrow  under president barrow the gambia's  government set up the truth  reconciliation and reparations  commission to probe allegations of jamai  era abuses  the panel heard from hundreds of  witnesses who offer testimony about  alleged human rights violations their  stories were broadcast on radio and tv  for the country to hear  the government now has six months to  decide its next steps we are hoping that  the government that has already given a  commitment that has made a commitment to  implement the recommendations of the  commission will make sure that free and  fair trials are held  right now there are recommendations for  prosecution but  of course they are just recommendations  and  the charges have not charges have not  been preferred against anyone so the  allegations are just that allegations  many at home and abroad hope to see the  former president on trial though he  remains in exile  but gambians weren't the sole targets of  the regime jaya james victims  include over 44 ghanaians who were  massacred they include nigerians they  include senegalese and the thinking is  that if all these countries  got together and helped gambia  to create a court it would also provide  the political  impetus  for  equatorial guinea where gia jammeh is  living  the commission is intended to promote  healing and reconciliation for victims  and survivors but jiame still retains  considerable support in the country  the possibility of his return from exile  was a key election issue earlier this  month  [Music]  and there are concerns his political  supporters could hamper efforts to put  the former leader and his associates on  trial  jammeh has yet to reply to the  commission's findings in the past he's  promised to return to the gambia but  he's been barely seen in the years since  his exile  the report may make him question whether  he would even want to  alexander lurch al jazeera
 

